From 801952de2f174558c24f4536b74f06277df78058 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axel Gneiting <axel@0m.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:52:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nak: Fix missing scoreboard for uniform Ldcg on SM120

The SM120 uniform register latency table puts Ldcg with
the other memory ops as decoupled. For uniform ops,
decoupled is replaced with Udp, which is fixed latency
and doesn't get a scoreboard. Ldcg reads memory through
the constant cache, so its latency isn't fixed. A user
of the result can read the register before the load is
done, e.g. an Ldcg using the address loaded by another
Ldcg.

Classify Ldcg as ToUr like uniform Ldc.

Fixes: 950465bdecd ("nak: add Ldcg")
Reviewed-by: Karol Herbst <kherbst@redhat.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45762>
---
 src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm120_instr_latencies.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm120_instr_latencies.rs b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm120_instr_latencies.rs
index 32c70014b5bc..e56b91b5d64c 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm120_instr_latencies.rs
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm120_instr_latencies.rs
@@ -255,11 +255,11 @@ fn op_ureg_latency(
         Op::ALd(_)
         | Op::ASt(_)
         | Op::Ld(_)
-        | Op::Ldcg(_)
         | Op::Ldsm(_)
         | Op::St(_)
         | Op::Atom(_) => decoupled,
         Op::SuLd(_) | Op::SuSt(_) | Op::SuAtom(_) => decoupled,
+        Op::Ldcg(_) => ToUr,
         Op::Ldc(_) => {
             if uniform_op {
                 ToUr
